media: camss: add SM8475 support

Add a separate SM8475 CAMSS resource table (six CSIPHYs, three CSID and
three VFE instances, the camera ICC paths) using the upstream CSID/VFE 680
operations, its DT binding, and the vendor CSIPHY v2.1.3 lane table decoded
from the shipped camera.ko (no public 2.1.3 sequence exists; the upstream
2.1.2 table was the bring-up substitute).

Note on the lane table: its records are byte-identical to the upstream
x1e80100 table except the four CSIPHY_SKEW_CAL words, which the driver never
programs (skew calibration is skipped).  It is kept until on-device
verification shows the upstream table streams; drop it then.

The camcc/gcc power programming that belongs with this node is in 0023/0024,
the board DT in 0022.

